Subject: Run Boost.Test's execution monitor under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: ports/patch/boost-filc.patch

The monitor installs handlers for SIGILL, SIGFPE, SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGPOLL,
SIGABRT and SIGALRM and an alternate signal stack before any test runs.
Fil-C keeps the default action for the four fault signals (sigaction fails
with ENOSYS, since the runtime reports those faults itself) and does not
support sigaltstack, so every Boost.Test program failed at startup with
"system_error produced by: exp: Function not implemented".

Under Fil-C, skip the alternate stack and leave signals whose handlers are
refused uncaught; the remaining handlers stay, so timeouts (SIGALRM) are
still reported as test failures. Covered by tests/boost-test.cpp in the
boost check phase.

diff --git a/boost/test/impl/execution_monitor.ipp b/boost/test/impl/execution_monitor.ipp
index 848670b..feaea52 100644
--- a/boost/test/impl/execution_monitor.ipp
+++ b/boost/test/impl/execution_monitor.ipp
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ namespace { void _set_se_translator( void* ) {} }
 // documentation of BOOST_TEST_DISABLE_ALT_STACK in execution_monitor.hpp
 #  if !defined(__CYGWIN__) && !defined(__QNXNTO__) && !defined(__bgq__) && \
    (!defined(__ANDROID__) || __ANDROID_API__ >= 8) && !defined(__wasm__) && \
-   !defined(BOOST_TEST_DISABLE_ALT_STACK)
+   !defined(__FILC__) && !defined(BOOST_TEST_DISABLE_ALT_STACK)
 #    define BOOST_TEST_USE_ALT_STACK
 #  endif
 
@@ -714,7 +714,17 @@ signal_action::signal_action( int sig, bool install, bool attach_dbg, char* alt_
         m_new_action.sa_flags |= SA_ONSTACK;
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __FILC__
+    // Fil-C keeps the default action for SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGILL and SIGFPE,
+    // since it reports memory-safety and hardware faults itself; sigaction
+    // fails with ENOSYS. Leave those signals uncaught and monitor the rest.
+    if( ::sigaction( m_sig, &m_new_action, &m_old_action ) == -1 ) {
+        BOOST_TEST_SYS_ASSERT( errno == ENOSYS );
+        m_installed = false;
+    }
+#else
     BOOST_TEST_SYS_ASSERT( ::sigaction( m_sig, &m_new_action, &m_old_action ) != -1 );
+#endif
 }
 
